# Hub-First Palette SSOT Migration

## Summary

Use the hub as the proving page for palette-only SSOT migration. Treat the current hub dark-mode neutral surface mapping as the local reference implementation, then move only those neutral fill values into shared theme tokens. Do not centralize structure. Do not touch immutable elements. Do not centralize semantic colors yet.

The migration target for this pass is:

- shared LM/DM neutral surface palette tokens exist
- hub consumes those shared neutral tokens
- hub keeps all structural ownership local
- no immutable or semantic color drift

## Implementation Changes

### 1. Establish shared palette primitives only

- In `web-asset/shared/portal-theme.css`, define palette-only neutral tokens for LM and DM:
  - page background
  - content background
  - panel background
  - card background
  - support background
- Keep these as raw color/fill primitives only.
- Do not define shared text, border, shadow, radius, spacing, or layout ownership tokens in this pass.
- Keep existing semantic and immutable color tokens unchanged.

### 2. Reduce hub to local aliases over shared palette

- In `web-asset/admin/portal-hub.html`, replace hardcoded local DM neutral fills with aliases to the new shared DM palette tokens.
- Keep hub-local ownership for:
  - layout
  - spacing
  - rail alignment
  - card geometry
  - icon placement
  - typography sizing/placement
  - breakpoint behavior
  - overflow clamps
- Keep the current hub-only dark page mapping behavior, but source the neutral values from shared tokens instead of local literals.

### 3. Preserve immutable and semantic color systems exactly

- Do not change or remap:
  - top header bar
  - footer
  - buttons
  - chips
  - pills
  - theme selector
  - icons
- Do not change:
  - admin/parent/student semantic card colors
  - semantic borders
  - washes
  - semantic text colors
  - shadows
- If any shared token attempt causes these to drift, back that token out and keep it local to hub.

### 4. Keep propagation blocked after hub

- Do not roll the palette into parent, student, or admin pages in this pass.
- This pass ends when hub is successfully consuming shared neutral DM palette tokens with zero non-surface drift.
- LM token formatting may be added in shared CSS now for parity, but LM pages do not consume the new contract until DM hub validation is complete.

## Test Plan

- Compare hub before/after at `320`, `390`, `768`, and `1280`.
- Validate that only these hub surfaces change through shared tokens:
  - page background
  - hero/section neutral surfaces
  - neutral support surface
- Validate no drift in:
  - card geometry
  - icon size/placement
  - text size/placement
  - header/footer alignment
  - prefooter button appearance
  - semantic parent/student/admin treatments
  - overflow behavior
- Smoke-check that parent, student, and admin pages still load and show no obvious palette regression.
- Regenerate `web-asset/shared/portal-theme.min.css` only after source CSS is correct.

## Assumptions

- The current hub local DM neutral palette is the approved baseline for centralization.
- Shared-token centralization in this pass is limited to neutral fills only.
- Any token that affects border, shadow, text, or immutable elements is out of scope and must remain local or unchanged.
- Structural normalization is not part of this pass, even if repeated patterns are observed.

